---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const jsonLd = [
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'WebPage',
    name: 'Terms of Service',
  },
];

const lastUpdated = '2026-09-12';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Service"
  description="Terms of service for LocalNodeOps benchmarks, guides, and calculators — an open-source hardware benchmarking resource."
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <article class="max-w-reading mx-auto px-lg py-2xl">
    <h1 class="text-display-hero text-primary">Terms of Service</h1>
    <p class="text-body-md text-secondary mt-xs">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

    <section class="mt-lg">
      <h2 class="text-headline-lg text-primary">Nature of the content</h2>
      <p class="text-body-lg text-secondary mt-sm">
        LocalNodeOps publishes hardware benchmarks, guides, and interactive
        calculators (such as the VRAM estimator) for informational purposes.
        Benchmark figures and calculator outputs are estimates based on
        published specifications and reference architectures — not
        guarantees of real-world performance for your specific hardware,
        model, or configuration. Verify critical decisions against your own
        testing before making a purchase.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-lg">
      <h2 class="text-headline-lg text-primary">Open-source content</h2>
      <p class="text-body-lg text-secondary mt-sm">
        Where a repository or code sample is marked open-source, it is
        provided under the license stated in that repository. Absent an
        explicit license, no permission is granted to redistribute site
        content commercially.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-lg">
      <h2 class="text-headline-lg text-primary">Affiliate and sponsored links</h2>
      <p class="text-body-lg text-secondary mt-sm">
        This site participates in affiliate/referral programs with select
        cloud GPU providers (currently RunPod and Lambda Labs). If you click
        one of these links and rent an instance, we may earn a commission
        at no additional cost to you. Affiliate links are only shown as a
        clearly labeled, separate suggestion when a calculated
        configuration exceeds the VRAM of the local hardware profiles
        listed on this site — never blended into the benchmark data or the
        VRAM calculator's output itself.
      </p>
      <p class="text-body-lg text-secondary mt-sm">
        The calculator's math (model weight size, KV cache estimate,
        runtime overhead, and which local GPU profiles a configuration
        fits) is computed identically regardless of whether an affiliate
        relationship exists with any provider, and is never adjusted based
        on affiliate revenue. See <a href="/methodology" class="text-accent-primary hover:underline">/methodology</a>
        for the exact formula.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-lg">
      <h2 class="text-headline-lg text-primary">No warranty</h2>
      <p class="text-body-lg text-secondary mt-sm">
        Content is provided "as is," without warranty of any kind. We are
        not liable for hardware purchase decisions, configuration choices,
        or outcomes based on information published on this site.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-lg">
      <h2 class="text-headline-lg text-primary">Changes</h2>
      <p class="text-body-lg text-secondary mt-sm">
        These terms may be updated as the site evolves. Material changes
        will update the "Last updated" date above.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
